.TH SFWC.CONF 5 "" "sfwc" "File Formats"
.SH NAME
sfwc.conf \- configuration file of the sfwc compositor
.SH DESCRIPTION
The file has
.B [section]
headers and
.B key = value
lines. Comments are lines starting with # or ; (inline comments are not supported, so #rrggbb
values are safe). Booleans are true/false, yes/no, on/off, 1/0. Mistakes never stop the
compositor: each is logged with its line number, the setting keeps its default and the rest
still applies. The file is re-read when it is saved (or with the reload-config action).
.SH SECTIONS
.TP
.B [general]
.B theme
(name, default),
.B terminal
(command used by $terminal),
.B focus
(click or follow-mouse),
.B mod
(Alt, Super, Ctrl or Shift: what $mod means; put it before the binds),
.B workspaces
(1 to 9, default 4).
.TP
.B [windows]
.B gap
(0-200),
.B decorations
(draw titlebars and borders),
.B snap_to_edges, snap_to_windows, snap_distance.
.TP
.B [keyboard]
.B rules, model, layout, variant, options
(xkb names),
.B repeat_rate, repeat_delay.
.TP
.B [output:NAME]
.B scale, position
(x,y),
.B enabled.
.TP
.B [animations]
.B enabled, open, close
(none, fade, fade-scale, slide),
.B move, duration_ms, easing
(linear, ease-in, ease-out, ease-in-out).
.TP
.B [templates]
.B enabled
and one boolean per template (waybar = false): render the theme's templates, see
.BR sfwc\-theme\-apply (1).
.TP
.B [keybinds]
.I modifiers+key
=
.I action
\(em modifiers are $mod, Alt, Super, Ctrl, Shift; the key is an xkb keysym name written unshifted
(Shift+m, not M). Having this section replaces all built-in binds. Actions:
.BR spawn:\fIcommand\fR ,
close, toggle-maximize, toggle-fullscreen, minimize, restore-minimized, cycle-windows,
move-to-next-output, focus-next-output,
.BR workspace:\fIN\fR ,
.BR move-to-workspace:\fIN\fR ,
reload-config, quit.
.TP
.B [mouse]
.I modifier+button
= move or resize (button Left, Right or Middle).
.TP
.B [autostart]
.B exec =
.I command
(one per line, started once with the compositor).
.SH EXPANSIONS
In spawn: and exec commands, $terminal, $theme (theme name), $runtime ($XDG_RUNTIME_DIR) and
$$ are expanded, as are theme placeholders such as @colors.background:hex@.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sfwc (1),
.BR sfwc\-theme\-apply (1),
the documentation in /usr/share/doc/sfwc (CONFIGURATION.md, THEMES.md).
